Fix https://github.com/medInria/medInria-public/issues/644

We can't quit a medRunnableProcess/QRunnableProcess naturally, but some checkpoints can be added in the running process to quit when reached.

When the user tries to close medInria, `medMainWindow::closeEvent` is sent, then `medJobManagerL::dispatchGlobalCancelEvent` emits a cancel signal, which is caught by `medRunnableProcess::onCancel`.

At the end, in `medAbstractProcessLegacy`  processes, `onCanceled` are run if it exists. Since we can't close directly the process, we can add checkpoints in the running method to test after or before some long algo if the signal has not been caught. For instance here in `medN4BiasCorrection::update` i added some:

```c++
 if (d->cancelAsked)
 {
        return medAbstractProcessLegacy::FAILURE;
 }
```

PS : i removed the _p file which was not necessary, i did not changed the algo, i just added the cancel tests.

